Our agency's on the verge of producing 
a star, and I'm only holding her back.

11:03.290 --> 11:06.770
You know that's not true. 
Ruby's getting work left and right—

11:06.770 --> 11:08.560
That's just luck.

11:09.780 --> 11:10.770
Seriously...

11:11.240 --> 11:15.510
We've been getting so lucky, it almost 
feels like someone's orchestrating it.

11:19.380 --> 11:21.450
I'm getting a lot of visitors lately.

11:22.290 --> 11:23.720
How'd you find me?

11:24.100 --> 11:27.660
Ruby keeps disappearing on her days off 
without telling anyone where she's going,

11:28.130 --> 11:29.630
so I followed her.

11:29.890 --> 11:32.500
You've grown up to be 
real weird about your sister.

11:33.070 --> 11:35.880
You're the one putting all those 
ideas in her head, aren't you?

11:36.600 --> 11:40.100
That's not all. 
You're getting her jobs, too.

11:41.390 --> 11:46.000
I'll never forgive you for leaving 
Miyako-san high and dry after Ai died.

11:46.440 --> 11:47.440
But...

11:48.340 --> 11:51.670
I'm starting to think you're still 
clinging to the Tokyo Dome dream.

11:53.300 --> 11:56.540
To the place where you and Ai 
were supposed to stand.

12:01.030 --> 12:04.720
You want to get back into 
idol management, right?

12:04.720 --> 12:06.000
Wrong.

12:06.420 --> 12:09.540
Yeah, I'm helping Ruby out with her work.

12:09.540 --> 12:11.920
I'm getting jobs from 
people I did favors for

12:11.920 --> 12:15.620
and people who sympathize with me 
because of what happened to Ai.

12:15.620 --> 12:17.880
I've got connections, after all.

12:18.520 --> 12:25.020
But I'm doing this because I feel bad 
for what I did to Miyako.

12:25.350 --> 12:27.480
I'm not clinging on to anything.

12:27.850 --> 12:30.480
If you still care so much 
about Miyako-san,

12:30.780 --> 12:34.980
why not just come back to Strawberry 
Productions instead of sneaking around?

12:34.980 --> 12:36.860
I've got unfinished business.

12:37.530 --> 12:40.200
I can't drag her into it.

12:40.200 --> 12:41.070
"Unfinished business"?

12:42.530 --> 12:44.840
You of all people should know.

12:45.630 --> 12:49.710
I need to murder the bastard 
who did that to Ai.

12:50.040 --> 12:53.170
But you were just her agent.

12:53.610 --> 12:55.130
Why go that far?

12:58.130 --> 12:59.300
<b>Ai's Fan for All Eternity!!!</b>

13:16.100 --> 13:20.030
Ai may have been your mother,

13:20.300 --> 13:24.000
but she was also like a daughter to me.

13:24.590 --> 13:25.720
Oh...

13:27.950 --> 13:29.470
I get it.

13:29.470 --> 13:32.460
That's why I went into showbiz, too.

13:34.380 --> 13:37.710
The mastermind was someone close to Ai.

13:38.470 --> 13:42.260
So I thought joining her business 
would get me closer to the truth.

13:43.320 --> 13:45.510
But here's the answer I found.

13:47.260 --> 13:50.350
The man who killed Ai is dead.

13:56.580 --> 14:00.080
I met someone who I shared 
paternal DNA with.

13:57.110 --> 13:58.110
<b>Private DNA Test Report

Result: It was determined that there
is a high possibility the individuals
are half-siblings who share the
same biological father.</b>

14:00.690 --> 14:02.360
<b>Bodies of Married Couple Found
In Apparent Double Suicide</b>

14:00.690 --> 14:04.160
Our dad was Seijuurou Uehara, 
and he's already gone.

14:04.670 --> 14:08.290
So our quest for revenge is over.

14:09.260 --> 14:11.290
There's no need to keep doing—

14:14.610 --> 14:15.630
Kid...

14:16.200 --> 14:17.590
What are you talking about?

14:18.160 --> 14:20.550
I remember that incident well.

14:21.120 --> 14:23.630
Plus when it happened, 
and how I found out.

14:23.760 --> 14:25.640
<b>Signs Point to Double Suicide</b>

14:23.760 --> 14:25.640
<b>Breaking:  Actors Airi Himekawa and Seijuurou Uehara Found Dead in Villa</b>

14:24.180 --> 14:27.290
It was when I was having a prep meeting 
with Ai for the Tokyo Dome concert.

14:25.640 --> 14:26.140
<b>Signs point to double suicide</b>

14:25.640 --> 14:26.140
<b>Breaking:  Actors Airi Himekawa and Seijuurou Uehara Found Dead in Villa</b>

14:26.140 --> 14:27.850
<b>Seijuurou Uehara, Actor</b>

14:26.140 --> 14:27.850
<b>Airi Himekawa, Actor</b>

14:28.140 --> 14:32.780
Seijuurou Uehara masterminded 
Ai's murder? That's impossible.

14:32.780 --> 14:35.680
He died before you guys moved.

14:35.680 --> 14:38.730
How could a dead guy 
have known your new address?

14:38.730 --> 14:41.370
The timeline makes no sense.

14:41.370 --> 14:43.250
But the DNA test...

14:43.250 --> 14:45.830
Did you consider the possibility 
of paternity fraud?

14:46.490 --> 14:50.990
The mother could've had the kid with 
a man other than her husband, you know?

14:50.990 --> 14:53.500
<b>Bodies of Married Couple Found In Apparent Double Suicide

A man and a woman were found unresponsive
in a cottage in Karuizawa. They were taken to
a hospital where they were declared dead.
A statement from the Nagano Prefectural Police
identified the deceased as actor Airi Himekawa
and fellow actor Seijuurou Uehara.</b>

14:51.320 --> 14:54.640
The Uehara deaths 
could've been a murder-suicide

14:54.640 --> 14:58.280
caused by an enraged husband who'd just 
found out about his wife's adultery, no?

14:59.130 --> 15:02.630
Before all that, why are you so convinced 
that your dad was the mastermind?

15:02.630 --> 15:06.000
Someone at the agency 
could've leaked the address, too.

15:06.510 --> 15:09.390
This isn't over. Not even close.

15:10.270 --> 15:13.380
You've always been a smart kid.

15:13.380 --> 15:17.260
If you'd thought about it for one second, 
you would've realized this yourself.

15:17.260 --> 15:18.230
And yet...

15:18.230 --> 15:20.820
You've got it wrong, Ichigo-san.

15:21.580 --> 15:24.820
You're overlooking something crucial.

15:25.140 --> 15:26.700
Something crucial? What's that?

15:26.700 --> 15:28.120
You have to be!

15:29.110 --> 15:31.410
There's gotta be something!

15:35.500 --> 15:39.420
It can't be... This can't be right.

15:40.110 --> 15:42.610
I was sure it was all over, finally...

15:43.950 --> 15:45.220
It's over, right?

15:45.220 --> 15:46.310
I mean...

15:46.310 --> 15:50.050
My bad. That was all just guesswork.

15:50.900 --> 15:54.160
You go home and get some rest.

16:06.320 --> 16:09.240
I've decided to start dating 
Akane for real.

16:16.170 --> 16:17.750
Sorry, let me off here.

16:26.010 --> 16:30.220
No... there's no way. It was all over.

16:30.860 --> 16:33.290
Ai's already been avenged.

16:33.770 --> 16:35.560
If not, then I...

16:35.560 --> 16:38.520
Isn't that great? We have our goal back!

16:39.710 --> 16:42.190
We can be driven by hatred alone,

16:42.720 --> 16:45.820
find the guy who killed Ai for real,

16:46.430 --> 16:50.450
and put him through all the suffering 
this world has to offer.

16:50.450 --> 16:51.160
<b>Ai's Fan for All Eternity!!!</b>

16:51.430 --> 16:53.620
I deserve to suffer.

16:54.270 --> 16:58.870
I have no right to enjoy my life 
after I let Ai die before my very eyes.

16:59.190 --> 17:01.960
This is punishment. Retribution.

17:01.960 --> 17:06.300
No! I finally got the chance 
to live my life!

17:06.300 --> 17:10.100
The peace you've had lately 
was just a passing dream.

17:10.100 --> 17:11.620
Forget about it.

17:11.620 --> 17:15.010
After all, we haven't put 
an end to anything at all.

17:15.010 --> 17:16.220
Take revenge.

17:16.480 --> 17:17.310
Get payback.

17:18.150 --> 17:21.730
Think of what Ai went through. Punish him.

17:18.930 --> 17:19.640
Aqua...

17:20.600 --> 17:21.730
Aqua?

17:22.060 --> 17:24.190
For what we lost forever!

17:23.100 --> 17:23.900
Aqua!

17:25.190 --> 17:26.190
Aqua!

17:26.190 --> 17:27.070
Shut up!

17:41.020 --> 17:42.500
Did I...

17:42.500 --> 17:45.710
Did I do something to make you 
hate me so much?

17:47.860 --> 17:51.630
I'm so stupid. I didn't have a clue.

17:52.290 --> 17:53.930
I'm so sorry, Aqua.

18:21.470 --> 18:23.120
<i>Hello? Aqua-kun?</i>

18:23.440 --> 18:25.250
Is now a good time?

18:25.930 --> 18:30.590
Oh, you've got the Japan Film Awards 
ceremony tomorrow, huh?

18:30.590 --> 18:34.430
Yeah, though I'm only one of the several 
rookie actor award recipients.

18:34.870 --> 18:38.180
Still, it's a red-carpet event! 
I'm getting nervous!

18:38.180 --> 18:41.400
<i>Even you still get nervous sometimes, huh?</i>

18:41.400 --> 18:42.770
Of course I do.

18:44.630 --> 18:45.730
So...

18:46.300 --> 18:49.630
Can we meet up tomorrow night?

18:50.410 --> 18:52.800
<i>It'll have to be quite late 
because there's a wrap party,</i>

18:52.800 --> 18:54.500
<i>but I want you to see the dress 
I'll be wearing—</i>

18:54.500 --> 18:55.460
Sorry.

18:56.570 --> 18:59.510
I kinda don't feel like 
seeing anyone right now.

19:01.030 --> 19:04.980
Really? Okay, I understand.

19:04.980 --> 19:08.030
If it ever gets too much, 
I'm always here for you, okay?

19:08.030 --> 19:09.980
<i>Thanks, Akane.</i>

19:09.980 --> 19:11.770
Sure. Bye.

19:12.460 --> 19:13.090
<b>Aqua-kun</b>

19:12.940 --> 19:15.930
<i>Aqua-kun had been in 
good spirits lately, too.</i>

19:13.090 --> 19:15.090
<b>Aqua-kun</b>

19:13.090 --> 19:15.090
<b>Call ended</b>

19:16.230 --> 19:20.510
<i>According to Ruby-chan, 
he wasn't always this gloomy guy.</i>

19:21.110 --> 19:24.600
<i>I bet things changed after Ai-san's death.</i>

19:25.080 --> 19:29.110
<i>Aqua-kun has panic attacks 
whenever he remembers her.</i>

19:29.480 --> 19:31.860
<i>His childhood scars 
always remain with him,</i>

19:32.280 --> 19:33.860
<i>almost like a curse.</i>

19:34.710 --> 19:40.280
<i>Now that he's free from avenging his 
mother, his guilt is fading gradually,</i>

19:35.860 --> 19:37.820
<b>Hey, that's mine!</b>

19:36.360 --> 19:38.070
<b>aah</b>

19:37.950 --> 19:40.280
<b>pout</b>

19:38.320 --> 19:40.280
<b>Just kidding.</b>

19:40.900 --> 19:43.870
<i>and he's becoming the person 
he was always meant to be.</i>

19:44.760 --> 19:46.940
<i>I can't help but hope...</i>

19:46.940 --> 19:51.910
<i>that he remains oblivious 
and lives a peaceful life.</i>

19:51.910 --> 19:53.680
<i>Then I'm sure Aqua-kun will...</i>

19:54.990 --> 19:58.830
With the acting chops 
cultivated by her years in theater,

19:57.380 --> 19:58.500
<b>Rookie Actor Award</b>

19:58.830 --> 20:01.850
Kurokawa-san has shone brightly 
in a variety of roles and productions.

20:02.310 --> 20:05.450
Congratulations on winning 
the Rookie Actor Award.

20:08.140 --> 20:10.610
I'm so happy for you.

20:10.610 --> 20:12.600
You're crying more than me.

20:14.110 --> 20:15.280
<i>Aqua-kun?</i>

20:15.950 --> 20:17.830
<i>Nah, there's no way.</i>

20:19.240 --> 20:20.240
Wow!

20:20.760 --> 20:23.210
The flower stand from the agency is huge!

20:23.210 --> 20:24.950
If not now, then when?

20:25.250 --> 20:28.770
Wow... the one from Lalalai is tiny.

20:28.770 --> 20:31.790
Times are tough for us 
theater groups, okay?

20:31.790 --> 20:33.460
<b>Celebrating the Rookie Actor Award
Theater Group Lalalai</b>

20:31.790 --> 20:33.620
<b>Celebrating the Rookie Actor Award
Akane Kurokawa-sama</b>

20:32.690 --> 20:35.820
White roses? Who are these from?

20:35.820 --> 20:37.340
A former member of Lalalai.

20:37.780 --> 20:42.550
He runs his own agency now 
and sends flowers any time we're involved.

20:42.980 --> 20:45.640
All kinds of people are 
congratulating me, huh?

20:45.990 --> 20:48.820
Never forget to stay grateful.

20:48.820 --> 20:50.350
Of course!

20:50.350 --> 20:55.070
Man, who'd've thought Akane would 
make such a rapid rise to stardom?

20:55.070 --> 20:57.940
It's all thanks to 
Kindaichi-san's coaching.

20:57.940 --> 20:59.100
Please.

20:59.100 --> 21:03.260
She's always had the skills, 
but in this business,

21:03.260 --> 21:06.190
you need to make a positive impression 
on the people with casting powers,

21:06.190 --> 21:08.410
or it's hard to land lead roles.

21:08.920 --> 21:13.380
President, your decision to put her 
on TV no matter what is paying off now.

21:13.860 --> 21:16.440
It seemed like an awful call at first,

21:16.440 --> 21:20.970
but ever since <i>Love for Real</i>, 
her public persona did a 180.

21:21.280 --> 21:23.210
What is it, the look in her eyes?

21:23.210 --> 21:25.950
She's usually so gentle,

21:25.950 --> 21:29.140
but when the cameras are on her, 
her eyes take on a glint like no other.

21:29.530 --> 21:33.470
You see people with eyes 
like that every once in a while.

21:34.050 --> 21:38.920
Eyes that trick people. 
The power to make lies seem like truths.

21:38.920 --> 21:41.600
For an actor, they're the ultimate gift.

21:44.980 --> 21:46.620
We had one of those in the past, too.

21:46.900 --> 21:48.890
Really? Who was it?

21:48.890 --> 21:51.220
The one who sent those roses back there.

21:51.220 --> 21:53.910
He was one of our best actors.

21:53.910 --> 21:55.340
I'd love to watch him!

21:55.340 --> 21:56.850
Do we have any footage?

21:58.420 --> 21:59.880
<b>Playlist</b>

21:59.380 --> 22:02.840
There's probably something in the 
oldest rehearsal video playlists.

21:59.880 --> 22:00.540
<b>Lalalai Rehearsal Recordings

17 subscribers</b>

21:59.880 --> 22:00.540
<b>Created playlists</b>

22:01.500 --> 22:02.840
<b>"The Starry God"
Unlisted
View full playlist</b>

22:02.090 --> 22:02.840
<b>Play all</b>

22:02.840 --> 22:03.800
<b>Rocking the Boat 1</b>

22:09.600 --> 22:10.810
He looks like him.

22:12.550 --> 22:14.100
He really looks like him.

22:14.830 --> 22:18.820
<i>Aqua-kun thought the mastermind 
was part of Lalalai.</i>

22:19.440 --> 22:25.560
<i>It was a guess based on the workshop 
Ai took part in before she got pregnant.</i>

22:25.560 --> 22:27.160
<i>That's not very conclusive.</i>

22:27.150 --> 22:32.660
<b>Bodies of Married Couple Found In Apparent Double Suicide

A man and a woman were found unresponsive
in a cottage in Karuizawa. They were taken to
a hospital where they were declared dead.
A statement from the Nagano Prefectural Police
identified the deceased as actor Airi Himekawa
and fellow actor Seijuurou Uehara.</b>

22:27.630 --> 22:32.440
<i>But what if Taiki Himekawa isn't 
actually Seijuurou's biological son</i>

22:32.440 --> 22:35.170
<i>but another man's child?</i>

22:36.670 --> 22:40.420
Himekawa-san and Aqua-kun's 
biological father

22:40.420 --> 22:45.970
could've very well been part of Lalalai, 
since Seijuurou and Airi were too.

22:46.910 --> 22:51.060
<i>Plus, his style of acting 
is very similar to Ai's.</i>

22:52.010 --> 22:56.230
<i>If Ai learned how to act 
directly from him...</i>

22:57.030 --> 23:00.570
<i>why has nobody ever mentioned that?</i>

23:02.040 --> 23:03.530
It was covered up.

23:03.610 --> 23:04.270
<b>Celebrating the Rookie Actor Award
Akane Kurokawa-sama</b>

23:04.750 --> 23:05.740
White roses.

23:05.730 --> 23:09.450
<b>The flowers the killer is thought to have brought,
white roses, were found strewn about...</b>

23:06.610 --> 23:09.450
The flowers the stalker had 
when he stabbed Ai...

23:09.780 --> 23:11.040
were also white roses.

23:11.780 --> 23:15.760
Somebody told a rabid fan 
that Ai had children, enraging him.

23:15.760 --> 23:18.670
He gave him Ai's address 
and incited the murder.

23:19.680 --> 23:22.920
He set the stage for it all to happen.

23:24.170 --> 23:28.890
<i>Ai's recreated emotions 
are stirring inside me.</i>

23:29.550 --> 23:31.370
<i>If it was him,</i>

23:31.370 --> 23:35.360
<i>I can see why Ai kept 
her partner a secret,</i>

23:35.360 --> 23:37.990
<i>and why he used someone else 
to commit the murder.</i>

23:38.990 --> 23:40.860
<i>More than anything, 
he looks just like him.</i>

23:42.180 --> 23:44.400
<i>His face and Aqua-kun's</i>

23:44.400 --> 23:45.840
<i>look so much alike!</i>

23:47.730 --> 23:49.240
<i>Hikaru Kamiki.</i>

23:50.170 --> 23:52.440
<i>When Ai got pregnant at sixteen,</i>

23:52.950 --> 23:55.500
<i>he was a fifteen-year-old middle schooler.</i>

23:55.490 --> 24:00.000
<b>Episode 28










Blind</b>

